&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customers and users across the globe use Planet&#39;s data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Image Quality Support (IQS) makes sure Planet&#39;s imagery meets that bar. We sit between imaging operations, satellite operations, software engineering, and the business — close enough to engineering to build our own tools, close enough to customers to know what &quot;quality&quot; means to them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Satellite Data Processing Engineer to help assess and automate imagery quality across Planet&#39;s satellite fleet. You&#39;ll split your time between hands-on visual QA and writing the software that scales it — a hybrid of remote-sensing know-how and software engineering, building up both with guidance from senior teammates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, hybrid role which will require you to work from our Berlin office 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact You’ll Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess satellite imagery, manually and via automated tooling, against contractual and technical quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and maintain the internal tools that power quality assessment — from QGIS-based QA tooling to backend scripts and data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support investigations into customer-reported quality disputes, gathering technical evidence for the team&#39;s decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the team&#39;s automated quality-assessment systems, helping shift routine checks from manual review into automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear reports and tickets that other engineering teams can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in geoinformatics, geomatics, remote sensing, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of optical remote sensing fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Python skills: comfortable with version control, code review, and writing more than one-off scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to QGIS or Python geospatial libraries (e.g. GDAL, rasterio, shapely).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic SQL / database familiarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication: you can explain a technical finding to a non-specialist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux comfort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitLab CI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any exposure to desktop GUI development (e.g. PySide6/Qt) or building small internal tools end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
